erms of use. Post such notification, it shall be your responsibility to review the updated Terms of use. Your continued use of the Incash platform following the posting of changes to the Terms of Use and the aforementioned notification shall be deemed to mean that you have reviewed the updated Terms of Use and accept and agree to the updated Terms of use.</p>\n<p>Incash reserves the right to terminate Your Account/this agreement and/or refuse to provide You with access to the Incash platform if it is brought to its notice or if it is discovered that you are not eligible to use the Incash platform.</p>\n<p>These Terms of Use shall be deemed to be an electronic record laying down the mutually acceptable terms for use of Incash platform by You. Being an electronic record generated by or through a computer system, it does not require any physical or digital signatures.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>DEFINITIONS</strong>  </li>\n<li>“ Employee” shall mean any person employed in full time confirmed service with the Employer, having a minimum service/employment history of 3 months with the Employer and a fixed salary.  </li>\n<li>“ Employer” shall mean any organization or entity whom employs the User Employee, with whom Incash has a separate agreement for facilitating extension of Salary Advance Facility from Incash to the User Employee and who has agreed to repay the Salary Advance Facility by debiting the salary of the User Employee, on behalf of the User Employee.  </li>\n<li>“ Transaction Fees” shall mean the charges payable by the User Employee to Incash for availing the Salary Advance Facility.  </li>\n<li>“ Products and Services” shall mean products, features, services, technologies, software etc. that are being offered on the Incash platform.  </li>\n<li>“ Repayment Account &#39;&#39; shall mean a bank account designated by Incash for collection of all the sum of money due to be repaid by the User Employees and wherein the Employer would deposit the said sums after deducting the same from the salary of the User Employee.  </li>\n<li>“ Salary Advance Facility” shall mean the amount sanctioned in the form of loan/credit facility as advance salary subject to appraisal by Incash and agreed to be disbursed to the User Employee as per the Salary Advance Facility Documents; irrespective of whether such disbursement is in whole or parts, as per the request of the User Employee through the platform belonging to Incash.  </li>\n<li>“ Salary Advance Facility Documents” shall mean the Agreements or any other document (as amended, restated or modified from time to time) executed by the User Employee/Employer with Incash for the grant of Salary Advance Facility, capturing the terms and conditions for the grant of Salary Advance Facility by Incash including but not limited to loan application, facility/loan/credit facility agreement, security documents, etc. or any other document stipulated by Incash from time to time.  </li>\n<li>“ User Employee” shall mean any Employee employed with the Employer, who are registered users of the Incash platform and have agreed to draw advance salary by availing Salary Advance Facility from Incash, on the basis of leads/reports generated by the Incash platform.  </li>\n<li><p>These Terms of Use set out the binding terms and conditions for use by a User Employee (“You”) of the Incash platform and the related Services as defined herein below.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS OF USE</strong>  </p>\n</li>\n<li>Incash platform along with the Products and Services are licensed and not sold (hereinafter together referred to as “the License”) to You for use only and solely in line with present Terms of Use.  </li>\n<li>This License is being provided by the Company ACCELETE NIGERIA LIMITED, a company incorporated under the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria and having its registered office at ,10th Floor, Eleganza Biro Plaza, 634 Adeyemo Alakija Street, Victoria Island, Lagos State. The terms Incash and the Company are used interchangeably in the Terms since Incash is a platform owned and run by the Company.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>4.     ACCOUNT CREATION</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>In order to use the Incash platform and Product and Services, you will be required to create an account (“Account”). As part of the Account opening process, you have to provide your name, gender, date of birth, age, phone number, photograph, other personal details, an e-mail address and a password etc. which is to be used for logging into the Account in the future. Further, in order to avail the Salary Advance Facility,   </li>\n<li>You will have to inter alia provide details including but not limited to your Employment Details (employee identification number with the Employer, official email id, bank details, proof of salary earnings or bank statement in the alternative, salary  and salary due date),  KYC details (,National Identification Number and a valid form of Identification.).  </li>\n<li>You hereby agree and undertake that you will not transfer or share your Account details and password with anyone. The confidentiality of your username and password is to be maintained by you as your sole responsibility and in case of any misuse or unauthorized access of the Account you shall be solely liable for the same. Further, in case of any such misuse or unauthorized access it would be your responsibility to immediately inform and notify Incash.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>5.     USER ELIGIBILITY AND THE CONDITIONS OF USE</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>You explicitly agree, represent and warrant that you:  </li>\n<li>can enter into legally binding contracts and have the capacity to enter into the present contract.  </li>\n<li>shall not give access to your respective Account to others or transfer Account to anyone else.  </li>\n<li>you or your Account has not previously been disabled by Incash for violations of its terms or policies.  </li>\n<li>are not prohibited from using the Incash platform or the Products and Service under applicable laws or orders/directions/judgments of courts.  </li>\n<li>shall not do anything that is unlawful, misleading, discriminatory or fraudulent.  </li>\n<li>shall not access or collect data from Incash platform using automated means or attempt to access data for which there is no permission to access.  </li>\n<li>shall not breach these Terms or any other Terms and policies that apply to use of Incash platform.  </li>\n<li><p>during the use of the Incash platform,  shall not provide any information is misleading or false in any way.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>AVAILING THE PRODUCTS AND SERVICES</strong>  </p>\n</li>\n<li>You may, after opening an Account on the Incash platform, apply for Salary Advance Facility by submitting your request on the Incash platform through a form on the Incash platform or through the Human Resource Manager of the Employer which shall contain the details of the proposed Salary Advance Facility including but not limited the amount, the date of repayment, mode of disbursement etc. (hereinafter referred to as the “Application Form”).  </li>\n<li>As a part of the application for Salary Advance Facility you shall be required to provide details and documents relating, including but not limited to, income, employment or professional status, such other information as Incash may require in terms of the KYC Regulations applicable to it (“Preliminary Information”).  </li>\n<li>You shall also be required to sign and execute the Salary Advance Facility Documents, as may be required by Incash, from time to time.  </li>\n<li>Subject to due diligence/approval by Incash, the Salary Advance Facility may be extended to You subject to your agreeing to pay the Transaction Fees as provided for in the Salary Advance Facility Documents.  </li>\n<li>You agree and understand that the Salary Advance Facility would be extended strictly in terms of the Salary Facility Documents executed between You and the Incash along with the present Ter